00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:08.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my name is chanya linghu  i am developing new technologies for  detecting the symphony of cellular  activities in the brain  the brain uses many different kinds of  simultaneously interacting signals to  function  all of these signals work together in  harmony in the healthy brain  to understand this harmony we need to  measure these signals at the same time  up to now most scientists could only  image one or two signals at a time  because the number of signal reporters  that can be used together  is limited to the number of available  colors on the microscope  we have just developed a new technology  that allows us to record multiple  signals in real time  regardless of the color of reporters we  call it signaling reporter islands  or series for short it works by  spatially separating the signal  reporters  into small islands throughout the cell  first  we engineered signal reporters to  self-assemble into serial islands in the  cell  next we record individual cellular  signals by capturing the light  emitted from individual series islands  then  we fix the cells and perform immune  staining to identify distinct tags bound  to each of the different reporters  finally we attributed the light  emissions to the corresponding cellular  signals  according to the immunosame results we  measured five signals together  in the first paper and we're working to  increase the number to tens of  individual signals  our hope is that by measuring multiple  aspects of the cellular symphony in  parallel  we can pinpoint the exact differences  between healthy and diseased brains  and provide insights into new treatments  [Music]

